From e218080e17a3845534ca8f265806648229549f86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jing-Ze Ma <jingzema0211@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 08:45:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rad_vet sc: a near-tangent chord samples the cells it crosses
 (sp and cs)

The closing segment of a curved-mesh ray took chi and S only at its ends: the upwind
point on the shell and the node.  A near-tangent chord, about sqrt(2 r dr) long, spans
several lateral cells, and an opaque cell between its ends was not seen, so its emission
was lost: E just outside a thick emitter was low by about 10 % and did not converge with
resolution or ray count (OPEN_BUGS #10; the lateral rays are the ones joining an emitter
to its lateral neighbours).  ScPathSeg integrates such a chord through the cells holding 2 sub-points per lateral cell
spanned (at most 16), chi and S constant per cell, where ln chi varies LATERALLY (within a
shell) along it by more than ln kVetCornerRatio; a radial change alone keeps the segment
rules (jump, split, corner).  The test before sampling is one pass over precomputed
bounds: ScSource stores per band cell the min and max of ln chi within 2 lateral cells
(vgd_cs components 2, 3), and ScLineRange reads them at checkpoints at most 3 cells apart
along the chord (never smaller than the sampled range, so the result does not depend on
the gate).  The samples stay inside the stencil's read window (a read beyond it is
clamped and counted, as the stencil's).  Spherical polar and cubed sphere alike.
Positive (all terms >= 0); closure only.

Clump deck (tau 20, 512 rays), E at 0-0.5 / 0.5-1 cell from the edge: sp -9.6 / -7.4 % ->
-7.8 / -4.1 %, cs -5.1 / -5.4 % -> -2.7 / -3.3 %.  1 vs 2 x 2 MeshBlocks in tile mode
unchanged (cs bitwise; sp 1 x 2 bitwise, 2 x 2 at round-off as before).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
